1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,630
Here is the view of central park from the rooftop of the hotel.
这是从酒店屋顶看到的中央公园景色。

2
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:13,880
It's pretty cool how you can see the contrast between the buildings on the right and then all the trees on the left.
很酷的是，你能看到右边的建筑和左边成片树木之间的反差。

3
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:22,230
City forest urban life rural life.
城市、森林，都市生活、乡间生活。

4
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:24,520
My parents are finishing up their breakfast.
我的父母正在吃完早餐。

5
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:28,600
My dad is really going all out with the buffet.
我爸爸在自助早餐上真是全力以赴。

6
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:37,270
Because it's included since I booked the hotel through american express so he is maximizing his time here.
因为我通过 American Express 订的酒店包含早餐，所以他要充分利用在这里的时间。

7
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:40,230
All right it's time to get some coffee.
好了，该去喝点咖啡了。

8
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:45,520
And let's see where we're heading follow the arrow we're going to go this way.
看看我们该往哪儿走，跟着箭头，我们往这边走。

9
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:51,230
It's a little bit cold out today partly cloudy.
今天外面有点冷，局部多云。

10
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:56,470
I think it's supposed to rain later so it might become overcast.
我想晚些时候会下雨，所以可能会变成阴天。

11
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:03,830
Overcast means that it's no blue in the sky and all gray.
overcast 的意思是天空看不到蓝色，全是灰色。

12
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:09,909
It's currently 10 44 a m so it's still before noon.
现在是上午十点四十四分，所以还没到中午。

13
00:01:09,919 --> 00:01:13,760
I don't know why there's always steam that comes out of those sewers.
我不知道为什么那些下水道口总是在冒蒸汽。

14
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:18,430
Does anyone know it kind of grosses me out when I walk over it.
有人知道吗？我走过它的时候会有点不舒服。

15
00:01:18,440 --> 00:01:26,270
We're on 5 th avenue which is a very popular long street with high end shops.
我们在第五大道，这是一条非常有名、很长的街，沿街有高端商店。

16
00:01:26,280 --> 00:01:28,990
High end meaning luxury.
high end 的意思就是奢华、高档。

17
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:35,750
We're now walking on madison avenue which is a lot less crowded compared to 5 th avenue.
我们现在走在麦迪逊大道，这里比第五大道没那么拥挤。

18
00:01:35,760 --> 00:01:41,160
The first thing I notice on madison avenue is there's a lot of banks.
我在麦迪逊大道上首先注意到的是，这里银行很多。

19
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:47,400
There's also a lot of businessmen walking around with their business attire.
还有很多穿商务装的人走来走去。

20
00:01:48,199 --> 00:01:51,390
Well I guess that's all of new York city actually.
不过，我想整个纽约其实都差不多。

21
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:56,909
There's my parents say hi.
我父母在那儿，打个招呼吧。

22
00:01:56,919 --> 00:02:04,070
There are many food delivery uh bikes they're usually on e bikes.
这里有很多送餐的自行车，他们通常骑电动自行车。

23
00:02:04,080 --> 00:02:13,280
Being an immigrant to the united states growing up I've always had the mentality of living to work instead of working to live.
作为一个在美国长大的移民，我以前一直抱着为工作而生活、而不是为生活而工作的心态。

24
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:20,040
So as I get older I'm really appreciating the latter mentality which means the second one.
所以，随着年龄增长，我越来越认同后面那一种心态，也就是第二种。

25
00:02:20,040 --> 00:02:25,670
That I mentioned which is you work to live.
我刚才提到的，就是你工作是为了生活。

26
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:32,430
That way I can enjoy my travels more and I can kind of turn off my brain when I'm on vacation.
这样我就能更享受旅行，度假时也能让脑子暂时放松下来。

27
00:02:32,440 --> 00:02:36,310
I don't always have to be thinking about work all the time.
我不需要一直想着工作。

28
00:02:36,320 --> 00:02:44,910
I'm also really grateful for my new haircut because my hair dried uh within like 20 minutes.
我也很庆幸自己剪了新发型，因为头发大约二十分钟就干了。

29
00:02:44,920 --> 00:02:47,110
I didn't have to use a blow dryer.
我都不用吹风机。

30
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:51,510
And it's perfect for someone who's always on the go.
这对总在外面奔波的人特别合适。

31
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,590
All right we need to cross the street.
好了，我们得过马路了。

32
00:02:54,600 --> 00:03:03,630
Hey do you recognize this I have the miniature version in my office that you might have seen during my live streams.
嘿，你认出这个了吗？我办公室里有它的迷你版，你可能在我的直播里见过。

33
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:10,460
I believe this is a kaws sculpture kaws is the name of an artist k a w s.
我觉得这是一个 KAWS 雕塑，KAWS 是一位艺术家的名字，拼作 K、A、W、S。
